# Review ownership for this repository.
#
# GitHub requests a review from the owner of every path a pull request touches.
# On its own that is a request and not a gate: the `main` ruleset has
# `require_code_owner_review` disabled, so a pull request still merges without
# the owner ever answering. This file is the half that has to live in the
# repository — enabling that toggle without it protects nothing, because there
# is no owner to ask.
#
# Last match wins. The catch-all comes first on purpose, and the paths below it
# are the ones that must not change hands silently when someone later adds a
# narrower rule for a package or an app. They decide what CI executes, what may
# reach a secret, and what is allowed to be pushed at all — a reviewer looking
# at a source change would not think to check them.

*                             @h-teske

# Everything CI runs with a token, including the composite actions the
# workflows call. A change here can widen its own permissions.
/.github/                     @h-teske

# The pre-push gate itself: the secret scan and the code review receipt. A
# change that weakens these also removes the check that would have caught it.
/agent-seed/                  @h-teske

# The secret catalogue and its audit rules — what a brokered request is
# allowed to resolve at all.
/packages/secret-contracts/   @h-teske

# What gets built, signed, published, and deployed.
/deploy/                      @h-teske
/.release/                    @h-teske
/.release-please-manifest.*.json @h-teske
/release-please-config.*.json @h-teske
/snapshot-policy.json         @h-teske

# The supply-chain floor: the minimum release age and `engine-strict` live in
# `.npmrc`, the resolved tree in the lockfile, and the update policy that feeds
# both in `renovate.json`.
/.npmrc                       @h-teske
/package-lock.json            @h-teske
/renovate.json                @h-teske

# The policies these owners are the ones enforcing.
/SECURITY.md                  @h-teske
/CONTRIBUTING.md              @h-teske
/AGENTS.md                    @h-teske
